  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the example is covered by a `{test}` reference. The test setup and assertions match its scenario, with two small gaps noted at the end.\n\n**Reference:** `tests/outcomes.rs` has one `{test}` reference to `requirements.ci.fixme_stale_input`, on `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` (line 204).\n\n**Setup:**\n- `fixture()` builds a record `requirements.timeout` with determination `{\"FIXME\": [\"#125\", \"rust-lang/rust#123\"]}`.\n- That record has a file-range input on `observed.txt` line 1, which is the comment `// FIXME(#125): …`.\n- The fixture is the same one that `fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` and `valid_fixme_remains_visible_in_status_info_and_book` use. Those tests show a FIXME record with a current input is valid and visible (`valid_fixme_remains_visible_in_status_info_and_book` also asserts the `#125` references show in status output).\n\n**Scenario steps:**\n1. The test overwrites `observed.txt` with `changed source`, so the recorded comment lines no longer match.\n2. `validate_repository` must then report an error containing \"input text changed\". That is the \"CI rejects the record because the recorded text no longer matches\" outcome. The record's determination is still FIXME, so the FIXME did not excuse the staleness (`requirements.ci.determination`).\n3. `status_markdown` must show the `requirements.timeout` row as `Invalid`, with `#125` and \"input text changed\" still visible. This confirms the changed input is reported while the FIXME is retained.\n4. Validation is a local, deterministic repository check. No model is involved and the gap is not reassessed.\n\n**Related cited requirements:** the test also adds a `{impl}` reference in `other.txt` and checks for a \"no input covers … other.txt:1\" error. That shows FIXME does not hide uncovered references either. The test carries `{test}` references to `requirements.ci.inputs` and `requirements.ci.determination`, which are the requirements the example cites.\n\n**Minor gaps:**\n- This test does not itself assert that the unmodified fixture validates cleanly. Other tests with the same fixture do.\n- It replaces the whole line rather than editing only part of the comment. That still changes the recorded text, so it exercises the same path.",
